@baseUrl = http://localhost:5081

### Process liveness; does not check SQL Server or Exchange
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Requires a client that sends Windows credentials (see Backend/README.md)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me
Accept: application/json

### Development only: real SQL connection; requires Windows credentials
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/diagnostics/database
Accept: application/json

### Current employee's theme; requires Windows credentials
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user-settings/theme

### Available active themes, ordered by DisplayOrder (requires Windows credentials)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/themes

### Save current employee's theme (no UserId/NTName in the body)
# Replace 2 with an actual themeId from GET /api/themes; display order is not the ID.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/user-settings/theme
Content-Type: application/json
X-CompanyPortal-Request: theme

{"themeId":2}

### Current employee's built-in card order; requires Windows credentials
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user-settings/card-order

### Save a complete order from GET; all active keys exactly once, no UserId/NTName
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/user-settings/card-order
Content-Type: application/json
X-CompanyPortal-Request: card-order

{"cardKeys":["library","inbox","email","requests","electronic-services"]}

### Authorized app choices for the signed-in employee
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications

### Personal cards, including currently authorized app memberships
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user-cards

### Create; replace appIds with IDs returned by /api/applications
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user-cards
Content-Type: application/json
X-CompanyPortal-Request: custom-cards

{"cardName":"تطبيقاتي","appIds":[1]}

### Replace with an actual userCardId from POST; IDs are not per-user counters
@userCardId = 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user-cards/{{userCardId}}

### Edit an owned card
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/user-cards/{{userCardId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CompanyPortal-Request: custom-cards

{"cardName":"تطبيقاتي اليومية","appIds":[1]}

### Soft-delete an owned card
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/user-cards/{{userCardId}}
X-CompanyPortal-Request: custom-cards

### Launch only after current grant check; replace 1 with an authorized appId
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/1/launch
